solvable:summary: openSUSE MicroOS
solvable:description: openSUSE MicroOS combines the benefits of a rolling OS with a read-only root filesystem with transactional updates. It is a modern Linux Operating System, designed for single-service installations, such as container hosts. It is optimized for large, clustered deployments.
        It inherits the benefits of openSUSE Tumbleweed while redefining the operating system into a small, efficient and reliable distribution.
