solvable:summary: Tools for loading replacement kernels into memory
solvable:description: Kexec is a user space utility for loading another kernel and asking the
currently running kernel to do something with it. A currently running
kernel may be asked to start the loaded kernel on reboot, or to start
the loaded kernel after it panics.
solvable:group: System/Kernel
solvable:license: GPL-2.0-or-later
