solvable:summary: Library of FUSE, the User space File System for GNU/Linux and BSD
solvable:description: FUSE (Filesystem in Userspace) is an interface by the Linux kernel
for userspace programs to export a filesystem to the kernel.

A FUSE file system is typically implemented as a standalone
application that links with libfuse. libfuse provides a C API over
the raw kernel interface.
